<%# Rendered only once the session has completed (see BatchConnect::Session
#render_completed_view / #session_completed_view in the OnDemand dashboard
source) -- this is why the success/error banner lives here rather than in
view.html.erb, which stops being rendered the moment the job leaves the
"running" state and OnDemand falls back to its own generic completed-session
partial instead.

Reads the pipeline_status file script.sh.erb writes next to output.log
(staged_root is a BatchConnect::Session accessor, in scope here because this
template is evaluated against the Session instance's own binding). %>
<%
status_file = staged_root.join("pipeline_status")
pipeline_status = status_file.file? ? status_file.read.strip : nil
%>
<% if pipeline_status == "SUCCESS" %>
  <div class="alert alert-success mb-0">Pipeline finished: <strong>Success</strong></div>
<% elsif pipeline_status %>
  <div class="alert alert-danger mb-0">Pipeline finished: <strong><%= ERB::Util.html_escape(pipeline_status) %></strong></div>
<% end %>
